    "source": "Kawasaki official specs + Wikipedia + Motorcycle.com first ride + Cycle World test",
    "notes": "H2R track-only variant. 998cc inline-4 with Kawasaki-designed centrifugal supercharger (two-speed drive). Bore x stroke 76.0 x 55.0mm = 998cc. Compression 8.3:1 (lower than H2's 8.5:1 for higher boost). Supercharger: centrifugal, two-speed drive, up to 2.4x atmospheric pressure (1.4 bar gauge). No intercooler (supercharger efficiency). Claimed 326hp @ 14,000rpm, 156Nm @ 12,500rpm. Ram-air at 330km/h adds ~10-15hp. Redline 14,000rpm. 6-speed close-ratio. 4-1 titanium exhaust. Single-sided swingarm. KYB AOS-II front fork with steering damper. Brembo Stylema monoblock calipers, 330mm discs. Rear: single-sided swingarm, 190/65 R17 slick. Weight 215.9kg wet. Fuel 17L. Track-only: no lights, mirrors, ABS. Rake 25.1deg, trail 110mm. Wheelbase 1450mm. 17L fuel. Ve_scale 1.15 accounts for supercharger volumetric efficiency. Boost: mechanical centrifugal supercharger (NOT electric_compressor), max 2.4x atmospheric. Two-speed supercharger drive. Ram-air at 330km/h adds ~10-15hp. No ABS, no mirrors, no lights - track only."
